  "outcomes": [
    "Design and implement Python classes using encapsulation, inheritance, and polymorphism, and explain why each data structure in this course is built as a class.",
    "Write, test, and debug Python programs that use functions and recursion.",
    "Implement stacks, queues, linked lists, binary trees, hash tables, and heaps from first principles.",
    "Analyze the running time of an algorithm using big-O notation and justify a structure choice by that analysis.",
    "Implement and compare simple and advanced sorting algorithms.",
    "Apply dynamic programming and greedy strategies to optimization problems.",
    "Represent graphs and apply BFS, DFS, and A* to reachability and shortest-path problems.",
    "Describe why parallel and randomized approaches are used in practice, with a working example of each."
